                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When you're investing in equipment for your business, you don't have time to sift through complicated charts or unclear details. You need straightforward answers. That's why understanding dry van trailer specifications matters. The right information helps you protect your bottom line, maximize payload, and make a confident purchase.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we work with owner-operators and fleet managers across Florida who want dependable equipment without unnecessary hassle. Whether you're expanding your fleet or replacing an aging unit, we can break down the key dry van trailer specifications in plain language.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-matter",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Dry Van Trailer Specifications Matter",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-matter"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-matter-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A dry van trailer is one of the most versatile and widely used trailer types in the trucking industry. A significant portion of freight rides in dry vans because they protect cargo from weather and theft while offering flexible capacity. But not all dry vans are built the same.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-matter-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>The wrong trailer size or weight rating can:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-why-matter-3",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Reduce your legal payload"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Increase maintenance costs"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Limit the types of freight you can haul"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Cut into your trailer ROI"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-matter-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Understanding specifications before you buy ensures you get equipment that works for your routes, customers, and long-term business goals.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
